{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":23,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":23,"text":"  verdict : SAMPLED MEAN IS 50 MS, COMPUTED CORRECTLY","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":24,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":24,"text":"","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":25,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":25,"text":"  averaging the real latency over every sample is the part","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":26,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":26,"text":"  done right here, and it is why 50 ms is the correct mean","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":27,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":27,"text":"  of the samples that were taken","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":28,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":28,"text":"","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":29,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":29,"text":"the sampling rule","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":30,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":30,"text":"  when a request is sampled : a clock tick lands while it","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":31,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":31,"text":"    is running","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":32,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":32,"text":"  so its chance of being sampled : is proportional to its","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":33,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":33,"text":"    duration","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":34,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":34,"text":"  a request twice as long : is twice as likely to be caught","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":35,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":35,"text":"  long requests, 2 percent of traffic : are 20 percent of","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":36,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":36,"text":"    the samples","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":37,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":37,"text":"  so the sample : is weighted by length, not one-per-request","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":38,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":38,"text":"","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":39,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":39,"text":"the result of the profiler","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":40,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":40,"text":"  reported average latency : 50 ms","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":41,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":41,"text":"  true per-request average : 20 ms","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":42,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":42,"text":"  milliseconds added by the length-bias : 30","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":43,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":43,"text":"  is the sample mean miscomputed : no; 50 is exact for the","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":44,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":44,"text":"    samples","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":45,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":45,"text":"  is 50 the per-request average : no; sampling by time","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":46,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":46,"text":"    over-weights the long requests","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":47,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":47,"text":"","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":48,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:assign","mono":48,"name":"nc_mean_sampled_by_time","value":"50","declares":true}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":49,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:assign","mono":49,"name":"nc_mean_sampled_by_request","value":"20","declares":true}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":50,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:assign","mono":50,"name":"nc_long_over_representation_per_myriad_removed","value":"2000","declares":true}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":51,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":51,"text":"null control - sample once per request, not per clock tick","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":52,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":52,"text":"  mean sampled by time : 50 ms","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":53,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":53,"text":"  mean sampled by request : 20 ms","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":54,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":54,"text":"  long-request over-weight removed : 2000 per myriad","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":55,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":55,"text":"  no request and no latency changed; each request stopped","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":56,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":56,"text":"  being weighted by how long it ran and started counting","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":57,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":57,"text":"  once","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":58,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":58,"text":"","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":59,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":59,"text":"what a mean of time-sampled latencies guarantees","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":60,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":60,"text":"  it is the correct mean of the samples : exactly, real","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":61,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":61,"text":"    latencies, every sample, honest average","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":62,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":62,"text":"  it is the average request latency : not addressed;","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":63,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":63,"text":"    sampling on a clock tick selects a request in proportion","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":64,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":64,"text":"    to its duration, so the long ones are over-represented","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":65,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":65,"text":"    and the mean rises from 20 to 50","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":66,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":66,"text":"","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":67,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":67,"text":"sampling by the moment favors whatever lasts longer, because a longer thing is in","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":68,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":68,"text":"more moments; the average that results is weighted by duration, and a per-item","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":69,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":69,"text":"question answered by a per-instant sample counts the big items more than once","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":70,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":70,"text":"","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":71,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":71,"text":"It averages the real latency over every sample - 50 ms is the exact sample mean.","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":72,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":72,"text":"But a request is sampled in proportion to how long it runs, so the long ones are","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":73,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":73,"text":"over-represented; sampling once per request gives 20 ms, the length-bias","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":74,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:output","mono":74,"text":"adding 6000 per ten thousand, until the sample is taken per request.","end":"\n"}
{"stream":"eml","proto":"eml-trace-v1","seq":75,"ts":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","type":"eml:run:done","mono":75,"ok":true,"outputs":63,"anomalies":0}
